Gcode generated bij LinuxCNC (Image to G-code) will move from X-max to X-min, with for every Y-movement also from maximum to minimum.
A lot of movements are not needed to go all the way to maximum or minimum Y-position to burn or engrave.
This (linux-batch) script will adjust those movements, so that only movemnts will be made that burn / engrave.
All additional movements will be removed.

LinuxCNC settings:
Scan pattern:    Columns
Scan direction:  Alternating
Tool Type:       Ball End
Roughing offset: 0.0

Script detects X1 (X-min), X2 (X-max), Y1 (Y-min) adn Y2 (Y-max).

For Y1 the script will rewrite all rules with 'G1 <Y1> Z0.0000' to 'G1 Z0.0000 ;; removed <Y1>' 
Next it will search 'G1 <Y1>' and grab following rule to check if it starts with G1, if not
  it will remark the G1 rule ';;' and place G1 on the followed rule.
Last Y1 adjustment is to rule out lines with only ' Y1' (to ';; Y1').

The same rules are applied for Y2, so:
For Y2 the script will rewrite all rules with 'G1 <Y2> Z0.0000' to 'G1 Z0.0000 ;; removed <Y2>' 
Next it will search 'G1 <Y2>' and grab following rule to check if it starts with G1, if not
  it will remark the G1 rule ';;' and place G1 on the followed rule.
Last Y2 adjustment is to rule out lines with only ' Y2' (to ';; Y2').

It also adds a remark section at the beginning:

;; ==========================
;;  LinuxCNC simplify script
;; ==========================
;; DG feb 2026
;; Script to simplify LinuxCNC movements of gcode
;; generated with the internal 'image to G-code' function.
;; Scan Pattern = Colums   Scan Direction = Alternating

Future should also detect movements without any Z-activity and rule them out?
For now the script works as designed.

DG.
